    },
    "image_with_text_tTRWBg": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_LawYNn": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How Foil Tapes Support Aerospace Applications",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_Uk4Bk3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Foil tapes are commonly used across the aerospace industry to address key operational challenges, including:</p><ul><li><strong>Aircraft Storage and Protection</strong><br/>Foil tapes help shield aircraft components from UV exposure, moisture, and environmental contaminants during storage, transport, and flight operations.</li><li><strong>Electrical Conductivity and Shielding</strong><br/>Copper foil tapes offer low electrical resistance, making them well suited for grounding, shielding, and protecting sensitive electrical systems.</li><li><strong>High-Temperature Resistance</strong><br/>Certain foil tapes are designed to withstand extreme heat and flame exposure, helping protect components in high-temperature environments.</li></ul>",
            "subtext_color": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_LawYNn",
        "text_Uk4Bk3"
      ],
      "name": "t:sections.image-with-text.name",
      "settings": {
        "container": "fixed",
        "color_scheme": "",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/enhace.png",
        "image_position": "left",
        "image_width": 50,
        "desktop_content_position": "center",
        "desktop_content_alignment": "left",
        "mobile_content_alignment": "inherit",
        "show_section_divider": false,
        "divider_width": "fixed",
        "padding_top": 0,
        "padding_bottom": 80
      }
    },
    "image_with_text_jcmPT6": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_hwz8FB": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Choosing the Right Foil Tape Material",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_KrHmTk": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Each foil tape material offers unique properties that make it suitable for specific aerospace applications. While all foil tapes provide valuable protection, selecting the correct material is essential for optimal performance.</p><ul><li><strong>Aluminum Foil Tape</strong><br/>Lightweight with an extended shelf life, aluminum foil tape resists corrosion from moisture, weather, UV exposure, and chemicals. It is commonly used to mask and protect aircraft components from harsh environmental conditions.</li><li><strong>Stainless Steel Foil Tape</strong><br/>A stable, non-corrosive material that provides added protection against heat, physical impact, and corrosion. Stainless steel foil tape is also used in industries requiring long-term durability, including food processing, marine, and nuclear applications.</li><li><strong>Copper Foil Tape</strong><br/>Known for its low electrical resistance, copper foil tape is ideal for electrical grounding, shielding, and cable wrapping. Its high malleability allows it to conform to complex surfaces, including low-surface-energy substrates.</li><li><strong>Lead Foil Tape</strong><br/>Available with rubber or acrylic adhesives, lead foil tape is well suited for high-temperature and radiation-shielding applications. It bonds effectively to most metal surfaces and can be <a href=\"/pages/die-cutting-and-material-converting-services\" title=\"Die Cutting and Material Converting Services\">die-cut into custom shapes</a> for assembly and manufacturing processes.</li></ul>",
            "subtext_color": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_hwz8FB",
        "text_KrHmTk"
      ],
